/-!
# Exact rank-four paid-packet containment

The concrete radius-two rank-four return has already discharged:

* every literal retained-head enclosure;
* every raw residual entry through physical mode 2048;
* the retained-coordinate and pole return of the rank-four reconstruction;
* the complete projected remote allowance through the 8192-mode tail recipe;
* the finite interval packet's signed quadratic theorem.

Its remaining finite premise is entrywise outward containment of the newly
calculated source-paid intervals in the stored 65-by-65 packet.  Both sides are
closed rational functions of the exact repository data.  This module states
that computation on the actual dependent carrier `Fin 64 ⊕ Unit`, splits it by
row, and asks Lean's kernel reducer to decide each complete row.

The row split is only a resource boundary.  It does not replace the source
matrix, round the calculated endpoints again, identify arrays by hashes, or
infer containment from the independent external screen.  Each theorem reduces
the exact declarations `RadiusTwoRankFourRemoteReturn.calculatedBounds` and
`RadiusTwoRankFourPaidPacket.bounds`.

A successful elaboration and kernel replay would remove the finite
packet-containment premise from the stage-one route.  The independent source
estimate

`OddLiteralWindow.HighFloor 2 (-1 / 2) (1 / 5) 64`

would still be required.  This file therefore asserts neither `StageLower 1`
unconditionally nor any cofinal, RH, or Dirichlet-GRH conclusion.

Primary mathematical mechanism: exact rational interval inclusion.  The
external arbitrary-precision screen recorded in grwtsk/noeaaeue reported all
8450 endpoint inequalities passing, but is diagnostic corroboration only and
is not imported as a proof premise here.  Independent analytical review and
novelty assessment remain pending.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

